{"seconds": 73.0, "exit": 0, "final": "After g4 Bh7+ Kxh7 Qxg4, Black has Qxf2+ or Nf3+, both giving check. Black is completely winning.\n\n**Coaching note:** \"This position is about recognizing that White's queen on h3 is both far from defending and vulnerable to attack. By playing g4, you force it to move or get captured. The key insight: when your opponent's piece is active but loose and far from support, attacking it with a pawn often works tactically. Here, g4 wins the queen by force because after Bh7+ Kxh7, the queen hangs on g4.\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"g4\", \"line\": [\"g4\", \"Bh7+\", \"Kxh7\", \"Qxg4\", \"hxg4\"], \"motifs\": [\"attraction\", \"hangingPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-forcing_lines", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23", "move": "g4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23", "move": "Nf5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23", "move": "Qd4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23", "move": "Qe3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3p2/pq1p1b2/3Pp1pp/2P1B2n/1P4PQ/P1N2P1P/1R3RK1 b - - 0 23", "move": "Ng2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r3r1k1/1p3